# Runtime environment for the Campus ERP container.
# Copy to .env.server and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Two different groups matter:
#   VITE_*  -> inlined into the browser bundle at `docker compose build` time.
#              Changing one needs a rebuild, not just a restart.
#   others  -> read by the Node server at runtime (restart is enough).

# --- Build time: browser-visible, safe to expose -----------------------------
# Leave empty to keep the values already committed in the repo's .env.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Runtime: server process only --------------------------------------------
# Same project as above; used by SSR routes and server functions.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Grants bypass-all RLS access. Keep it out of every VITE_* variable, or it
# ships inside publicly downloadable JavaScript.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Runtime: tuning ---------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000
# NODE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Runtime: attendance persistence -----------------------------------------
# Where the Node server keeps live QR sessions, records and class rosters.
# Already set to /data in the image, which the `eqr-data` volume mounts; override
# only for a bind mount or a local `node .output/server/index.mjs` run.
# DATA_DIR=/data

# Attendance reaches Supabase only when BOTH values above and a service role key
# are present, and when supabase/migrations/20260930090000_attendance_mirror_tables.sql
# has been applied. Without them the server store is the only copy — still shared
# across every device, but confined to this container's /data volume.
